## Why CC BY-SA

Bare facts — who won a race, how long a circuit is — are not copyrightable,
and a database of those facts would be free to license under anything. But
this database also contains prose taken from or closely following Wikipedia
articles: the car design histories, circuit descriptions, and some notes and
glossary entries. Wikipedia text is licensed CC BY-SA 4.0, and that prose
carries the same attribution and share-alike requirements with it. Rather
than draw a line field-by-field, the whole data release is licensed CC BY-SA
4.0 — with the one exception in the next section, where the line is drawn
because there was never anything on the other side of it. See ATTRIBUTION.md
for the source of every part of the data and the reasoning in full.

