  - `known_gaps.area`, `known_gaps.reader`, `known_gaps.description` and
    `known_gaps.resolution` — what a reader is shown about each gap, the
    maintainer's note on it, and what would close it.

Attribute Lap Ledger; there is no share-alike, so
nothing you build on them takes a licence from them. The share-alike above
comes from Wikipedia, and none of Wikipedia's text is in these columns: every
sentence in them was written for this project, about this project's own
database. The remaining columns of those two tables — the subject and field
of a disagreement, the two values, the state of a gap, the number of races it
affects — hold facts and identifiers rather than expression.

The grant is stated inside the database too, as `meta.project_prose` and
`meta.project_prose_columns`, so a copy of `f1.db` carries its own terms; a
build in which those disagree with this file fails. A CC BY grant cannot be
withdrawn from a copy already taken, which is why the list is exactly this
long.

**The rest of the project's own prose is not in it yet.** `source_registry`
